    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="faq">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">09 &mdash; FAQ</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-6">Frequently asked questions</h2>

        <div class="space-y-2">
          <div class="faq-item bg-card border border-border rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
            <button class="faq-q w-full text-left px-5 py-4 flex items-center justify-between gap-4 cursor-pointer bg-transparent border-none">
              <span class="text-[15px] font-semibold text-ink leading-[1.4]">Can I use UGC content indefinitely if I paid the creator a flat fee?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon text-accent text-[18px] font-bold shrink-0 select-none">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-a max-h-0 overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out">
              <div class="px-5 pb-4 text-[14px] text-ink-2 leading-[1.6]">No. A flat production fee covers the creation of the content, not unlimited usage rights. Unless your contract explicitly grants perpetual usage, the license has a default expiration. Many creators assume organic-only usage when no license is specified. If you want perpetual rights, negotiate and pay for them separately. Running content beyond the licensed period is a breach of contract and potentially a copyright infringement.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item bg-card border border-border rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
            <button class="faq-q w-full text-left px-5 py-4 flex items-center justify-between gap-4 cursor-pointer bg-transparent border-none">
              <span class="text-[15px] font-semibold text-ink leading-[1.4]">What happens if a creator uses copyrighted music in my UGC video?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon text-accent text-[18px] font-bold shrink-0 select-none">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-a max-h-0 overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out">
              <div class="px-5 pb-4 text-[14px] text-ink-2 leading-[1.6]">Both the creator and the brand can face liability. The platform will likely flag or remove the content, and in paid advertising, the music rights holder can pursue the advertiser directly. Your contract should include a representations clause where the creator warrants that all content elements are original or properly licensed, plus an indemnification clause that shifts liability to the responsible party. Proactively, provide creators with a list of approved royalty-free music sources.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item bg-card border border-border rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
            <button class="faq-q w-full text-left px-5 py-4 flex items-center justify-between gap-4 cursor-pointer bg-transparent border-none">
              <span class="text-[15px] font-semibold text-ink leading-[1.4]">Do FTC disclosure rules apply if I only use UGC as paid ads, not organic posts?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon text-accent text-[18px] font-bold shrink-0 select-none">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-a max-h-0 overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out">
              <div class="px-5 pb-4 text-[14px] text-ink-2 leading-[1.6]">Yes. The FTC&rsquo;s disclosure requirements apply to any endorsement where a material connection exists, regardless of the distribution method. When a creator&rsquo;s testimonial runs as a paid ad, the audience still sees what appears to be a genuine endorsement. The &ldquo;Sponsored&rdquo; label that platforms add to paid ads helps, but it does not replace the need for disclosure within the content itself, particularly for video ads where the endorsement is verbal.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item bg-card border border-border rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
            <button class="faq-q w-full text-left px-5 py-4 flex items-center justify-between gap-4 cursor-pointer bg-transparent border-none">
              <span class="text-[15px] font-semibold text-ink leading-[1.4]">How do I handle content rights when working with creators in the EU?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon text-accent text-[18px] font-bold shrink-0 select-none">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-a max-h-0 overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out">
              <div class="px-5 pb-4 text-[14px] text-ink-2 leading-[1.6]">EU creators retain moral rights that cannot be transferred or waived in most member states. This means even with a full buyout, the creator can object to uses that damage their reputation. Structure your agreements to license economic rights broadly while respecting moral rights. Also ensure GDPR compliance for any personal data you collect from EU creators during onboarding. Specify the governing law in the contract &mdash; without it, a court may apply the creator&rsquo;s local law, which may be less favorable to the brand.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item bg-card border border-border rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
            <button class="faq-q w-full text-left px-5 py-4 flex items-center justify-between gap-4 cursor-pointer bg-transparent border-none">
              <span class="text-[15px] font-semibold text-ink leading-[1.4]">Can OKAD help set up legally compliant UGC workflows?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon text-accent text-[18px] font-bold shrink-0 select-none">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-a max-h-0 overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out">
              <div class="px-5 pb-4 text-[14px] text-ink-2 leading-[1.6]">Yes. We manage the full legal and operational pipeline for brands running UGC at scale &mdash; from contract templates and creator onboarding to compliance review and rights tracking. We work with over 700 creators across the US, EU, and UK, so our agreements are built to handle multi-jurisdiction requirements. Write to us at <a href="mailto:olga@okad.agency" class="text-accent hover:underline">olga@okad.agency</a> or <a href="https://calendly.com/okad_calls/first" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent hover:underline">book a call</a> to discuss your program.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

